  "note": "East at the right. yui on the west shore of Suruga Bay under the Satta headland, Fuji across the water (drawn on the sheet: the lie of the land); osaka at its river mouth west of the Kii peninsula's bulge (PAINT-21F: a place now; its castle has walls and turrets and no keep); hills north of Osaka (the hollow in the wooded hills: cedars and the storehouse); akashi on the shore above its strait, Awaji across it (PAINT-21F); himeji at the west end on its hill above the town, the Inland Sea below; shosha north-west of Himeji, a wooded mountain with the women's hall at its foot (PAINT-21F). The sea way goes out from Yui's shore round the Kii tip into Osaka's bay (a ship drawn on it); the river path goes up the Yodo to Hirakata (the Kyoto boat drawn on it), across by the ferry at Hirakata and north into the hills (`river`: where the water ends; the stop `hirakata` there); the road west comes down by Koriyama, round to Nishinomiya and along the shore by Suma and Maiko to Akashi (`stops`: each a picture with its `pin`, the point of its way's line it is for, where the portraits stop: for the walk's three, where their row stands just above the picture, the line said above them; Hirakata's at the river's turn; and a `label`, its name's baseline middle, for a name written at the map's size less 3, as the engine writes a stop's); the road on to Himeji; the walk between Himeji and Shosha. Each via is a pin, the way's drawn points, the other pin. The pins (rows of three portraits, 116 x 36) stand beside each place (Osaka's on the sea east of it)."
